{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfgDApnnW2cDb5uCH2ToW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe split into a dedicated immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` record plus a single `primaryIdentifier` resolution point is a good, idiomatic shape, and `AuditOwnerCreated` stays a thin two-method unit. One structural issue keeps it from being clean:\n\n**The event's own discriminator is threaded through the caller.** `OWNER_CREATED` is an intrinsic property of what an `OwnerCreatedEvent` *is*, yet the record accepts it as a constructor component and the caller passes `OwnerCreatedEvent.OWNER_CREATED` back into `new OwnerCreatedEvent(...)`. That round-trip is redundant and lets the type be constructed with an inconsistent `event` value. The record should own this itself — e.g. a convenience constructor that omits `event` and fills it, or a compact/canonical constructor that always sets it — so Jackson still serializes the `event` field but no caller can (or has to) supply it. That also removes the need for the public `OWNER_CREATED` constant to be part of the call site.\n\nSecondary, worth a second look but defensible under the current spec:\n\n- The record component and JSON key are named `customerCode`, but the value is sourced from `primaryIdentifier(owner)` and the javadoc promises that flipping that method alone makes the event \"carry the memberId.\" Structurally the value and the field name will then disagree (a `customerCode` key holding a memberId), which undercuts the \"change only one point\" claim for anyone reading the emitted JSON. The field name is correct for today's spec, so this is a latent coherence risk to flag rather than a blocker — just make sure the eventual memberId change is understood to touch the field name too, not only `primaryIdentifier`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10293,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10293},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01c1bd2b-7be0-49a6-99ce-519b72623417","uuid":"f285def7-89b4-45d7-899f-3291628fa460","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:58:51.472Z","request_id":"req_011CfgDApWfCCPS3emdFyLem"}
